    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **274 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented a daily owner-registration cap of 20 on `POST /api/owners`, rejecting the 21st create of the day with **400 Bad Request**.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, I added:\n\n1. **`CheckDailyRegistrationLimit.java`** (function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today (`LocalDate.now()`); throws `DailyRegistrationLimitException` when the count reaches 20. Runs *before* save, so it doesn't count the owner being created.\n\n2. **`DailyRegistrationLimitException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it appears in the `throws` clause and can be escalated.\n\n3. **`DailyRegistrationLimitExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `DuplicateOwnerExceptionHandler` (which returns 409).\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DailyRegistrationLimitException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `checkDailyLimit` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) right after `build`, so the registration date is set before the count.\n\nThe new `Cp13Tests` acceptance test (20 successful creates, 21st expects 400) passes, and all existing tests remain green.",
